#### A Compact K-means Workflow

It is convenient to keep the main steps in one code chunk. Change only the value of number of `centers` and re-run the chunk:

```{r}
set.seed(123)

# 1. Run k-means
km <- kmeans(
  cluster_data_scaled,
  centers = 3,
  nstart = 25
)

# 2. Visualize the result
fviz_cluster(
  km,
  data = cluster_data_scaled,
  geom = "point",
  ellipse.type = "convex",
  ggtheme = theme_minimal()
)
```



